ock pays off, but the gain is small.\n\n**Comparing the two-day plans and candidate 0:**\n- **Candidate 3** orders about 1.046 × forecast, which is exactly the average demand.\n- **Candidate 6** orders about 1.08–1.09 × forecast. On item 0 it buys about 40 extra units and carries extra stock; the sales it rescues don't pay for that. On item 1 the gain is roughly zero. Net, it trails candidate 3 by roughly 100–200.\n- **Candidate 4** orders about 1.2–1.25 × forecast. Surplus piles up, ends unsold and pays holding, so it is clearly worse.\n- **Candidate 0** saves about 96 by ordering on only 12 days. But it orders about 1.15 × forecast, which means roughly 75 extra units of item 0 plus holding, so it loses several hundred overall.\n\nIf actual demand differs from the forecast, candidate 3 stays the most stable: its surplus has no built-in growth, and every delivery is a short two-day batch."}], "container": null, "stop_reason": null, "stop_sequence": null, "stop_details": null, "usage": {"input_tokens": 2, "cache_creation_input_tokens": 356, "cache_read_input_tokens": 5754, "cache_creation": {"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens": 0, "ephemeral_1h_input_tokens": 356}, "output_tokens": 8, "service_tier": "standard", "inference_geo": "global", "speed": "standard"}, "input_transformations": [], "diagnostics": null, "context_management": null}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "timestamp": "2026-10-26T08:21:15.896Z", "request_id": "req_011CgQX9mYYmFhK2ixjDkHTT"}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_stop", "index": 1}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "stream_event", "event": {"type": "content_block_start", "index": 2, "content_block": {"type": "tool_use", "id": "toolu_01B2EKpQaKEJmvA2nKQmDvgz", "name": "StructuredOutput", "input": {}, "caller": {"type": "direct"}}}, "parent_tool_use_id": null}, {"type": "assistant", "message": {"model": "claude-opus-5-5", "id": "msg_011CgQX9mnvmioxeD9T6Zn5T", "type": "message", "role": "assistant", "content": [{"type": "tool_u